# -*- coding: utf-8 -*-
"""
Layer-1 curated data, part A: the chemical inventory ("what's on the shelf").

Conventions
  compact record  = (id, NAME, FORMULA, state, colour, note_dict)
  state  : s solid | l liquid | g gas | aq aqueous solution | v viscous/oily l
  colour : plain word the renderer can map to a hex (see reference.json colour_map)
  note keys:
    mp, bp            degrees C (curated, high confidence)   None = not curated here
    den               g/cm3 (20-25 C unless stated)
    ion               'Fe3+' the species releases as its dominant aqueous ion
    ka / kb           list of pK values (polyprotic, in order)
    role              acid | base | ampho | neutral | oxidiser | reducer | complexer
    e                 'Zn2+/Zn' standard reduction pair id (see electrochem)
    dhf               dict state->kJ/mol formation enthalpy ('s','l','g','aq')
    sol               solubility in water, g/100 g at ~20 C (None = insoluble)
    solv              {'ethanol':'s', 'ether':'s', ...} s=soluble sl=slight i=insoluble
    hygro             hygroscopic/deliquescent
    vol               volatile (opens a bottle and you smell it)
    odour            words
    stock             {label, conc_pct, den, molarity} commercial bottle
    hydrate           parent id of the anhydrous form
    flame             flame-test colour (elements/salts)
    forms             physical form for elements
    gas_id            for a solution, the solute gas id
    cas               CAS registry number (only where I'm certain of it)
    danger            0 low 1 wear gloves/goggles 2 fume hood/careful 3 sim restricts
"""

